HelloAROS is a two-source native C project.

From an AROS Shell:
  CD Development:Examples/HelloAROS
  make all
  make run
  make clean

make -j4 also works. The Makefile uses the packaged shell, compiler and SDK
through Development:, so the build does not depend on the Shell current PATH.
Errors retain Clang file:line:column locations. Build and run failures propagate
through make. The program checks that sum(1..100) is 5050 and returns 20 on failure.
